          "@id": "pkg:apk/dhi/dotnet8-runtime@8.0.31-r0?distro=dhi-3.23"
        }
      ],
      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "Update dotnet8-runtime to 8.0.32-r0 or later.",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-58280 (GHSA-mc4q-93x5-f6hj) is a .NET denial of service issue in signed XML processing (System.Security.Cryptography.Xml and System.Private.Xml): crafted input can cause uncontrolled recursion and excessive resource use. Microsoft lists Windows, Linux and macOS as affected platforms and the .NET 8.0 runtime packs, including linux-musl-x64 and linux-musl-arm64, as affected from 8.0.0 through 8.0.31 and fixed in 8.0.32 (https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-mc4q-93x5-f6hj, https://github.com/dotnet/announcements/issues/447, https://github.com/dotnet/core/blob/main/release-notes/8.0/8.0.32/8.0.32.md). DHI dotnet8-runtime for Alpine 3.23 builds .NET 8 for Linux from Microsoft's source release, and each build's version is the .NET runtime version it carries. Scanned all 220 packages of the ten published builds (8.0.23-r0, 8.0.24-r0, 8.0.25-r0, 8.0.26-r0, 8.0.27-r0, 8.0.29-r0, 8.0.31-r0, 8.0.32-r0, 8.0.33-r0 and 8.0.34-r0) for x86_64 and aarch64, including the debug packages and the files inside the nupkg, zip and tar.gz archives they hold. Implementation copies of System.Security.Cryptography.Xml.dll are in the Microsoft.AspNetCore.App shared framework (aspnetcore8-runtime, and the .NET SDK held by dotnet8-runtime-bootstrap), the SDK's own and F# copies and the ASP.NET Core runtime pack in dotnet8-runtime-bootstrap, and, in dotnet8-runtime-artifacts, the System.Security.Cryptography.Xml nupkg (net8.0 and netstandard2.0) and the ASP.NET Core and WindowsDesktop transport nupkg files: nine per build and architecture. System.Private.Xml.dll is in the Microsoft.NETCore.App shared framework of dotnet8-runtime and of the .NET SDK held by dotnet8-runtime-bootstrap, and in the runtime pack and the NativeAOT compiler pack held by dotnet8-runtime-bootstrap: four per build and architecture. Every one of these copies carries the build's own .NET version and records the matching dotnet/runtime release commit (for example the v8.0.31 commit in 8.0.31-r0 and the v8.0.32 commit in 8.0.32-r0): 8.0.23 to 8.0.31 in the first seven builds and 8.0.32 or later from 8.0.32-r0 on, on both architectures. The other copies are reference assemblies with no implementation code. The range ends at 8.0.32-r0 because it is the first published build with the fix."
    },
